    "publisher": "Charles Scribner's Sons",
    "pageCount": "98",
    "description": "Drawing Made Easy has taught millions of people how to draw. The book uses a sensible approach. Each drawing begins with simple, easy-to-comprehend shapes and proceeds to details\r\n  last, essentially the same method used in the 19th century academies. Each drawing is presented in a series of straightforward and memorable stages. The subjects are people, animals, flowers, and\r\n  charmingly antique trains and cars. The beginning student—either child or adult—progresses to fairly challenging subjects by the end."
